==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|certaine||obsolete}}
* {{alter|en|certayne||archaic}}
* {{alter|en|certeine||archaic}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*krey-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|certeyn}}, {{m|enm|certein}}, {{m|enm|certain}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|certain}}, from a {{der|en|VL.|-}} unattested form {{m|la|*certānus}}, extended form of {{der|en|la|certus||fixed, resolved, certain}}, of the same origin as {{m|la|cretus}}, past participle of {{m|la|cernere||to separate, perceive, decide}}. Displaced native {{cog|enm|-}} {{m|ang|wis}}, {{m|ang|iwis||certain, sure}} (from {{cog|ang|ġewiss||certain, sure}}) and alternative {{cog|enm|-}} spelling {{m|enm|sertane||some, certain}}.

